# =============================================================================
# 3. MESSAGES  (phase 2 — a CURATED batch of high-visibility status/error text)
# =============================================================================
# Status-line and error text. These carry NAMED {placeholders} (not positional
# {}) so a translation may reorder the pieces; keep every {name} intact.
#
# Only the most-seen messages are routed through the catalog so far. The long
# tail (~200 script-parser diagnostics from the XPL engine) stays English — they
# reference command VERBS, which are the command language, not UI chrome. Two
# grep messages that pluralize inline ("N match/matches in M file/files") are
# also still English, pending a pluralization convention.

msg.search.not_found = ei löytynyt: {find}   # not found: {find}
msg.open.not_found = tiedostoa ei löytynyt: {path}   # file not found: {path}
msg.save.written = tallennettu {name}   # saved {name}
msg.readonly = asiakirja on vain luku -tilassa (RO avaa lukituksen)   # document is read-only (RO to unlock)
msg.grep.none = GREP: ei osumia   # GREP: no matches
msg.grep.searching = GREP: etsitään…   # GREP: searching…
